      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Can confirm. It feels needless that HUD opacity would affect the face mirror, as the face mirror has its own opacity slider and is generally very separate from the HUD settings. If you want something like gesture icons and invite icons to be very transparent but you like your face mirror to be at 100% for best visibility, currently, you can't do that, even though the face mirror has its own setting.\nAt low enough HUD opacity, the face mirror becomes entirely unusable while HUD icons are simple enough that they would still work. The mic icon isn't affected by HUD opacity either because it has its own slider, so the face mirror should be the same.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
